{number: 89}
{title: All the Way My Saviour Leads Me}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] All the way my Savior leads me;
What have I to ask be-[G7] side?
Can I [C] doubt His tender [F] mercy,
Who through [C] life has [G7] been my [C] Guide?
Heav'nly [F] peace, divinest [C] comfort,
Here by [G7] faith in Him to [C] dwell!
For I [F] know, whate'er be-[C] fall me,
Jesus [G7] doeth all things [C] well;
For I [F] know, whate'er be-[C] fall me,
Jesus [G7] doeth all things [C] well.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] All the way my Savior leads me,
Cheers each winding path I [G7] tread,
Gives me [C] grace for every [F] trial,
Feeds me [C] with the [G7] living [C] bread.
Though my [F] weary steps may [C] falter,
And my [G7] soul athirst may [C] be,
Gushing [F] from the Rock be-[C] fore me,
Lo! A [G7] spring of joy I [C] see;
Gushing [F] from the Rock be-[C] fore me,
Lo! A [G7] spring of joy I [C] see.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] All the way my Savior leads me,
Oh, the fullness of His [G7] love!
Perfect [C] rest to me is [F] promised
In my [C] Father's [G7] house a-[C] bove.
When my [F] spirit, clothed im-[C] mortal,
Wings its [G7] flight to realms of [C] day,
This my [F] song through endless [C] ages:
Jesus [G7] led me all the [C] way;
This my [F] song through endless [C] ages:
Jesus [G7] led me all the [C] way.
{end_of_verse}
